course: dictionary
lesson: 10277
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word torch can mean a small light you hold in your hand, a stick with a flame on top, or to set something on fire. The words around it tell you which meaning is right, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: «In a power cut, use a torch, not a candle, keep the fridge closed, and never touch a fallen line.» The power cut and the candle tell you the torch is a light you hold in your hand. Try the meaning in the sentence: does "use a flame on a stick" fit a power cut? Not as well as a small battery light does.
explain: «Many pass the Statue of Liberty, a giant statue holding up a torch.» Holding up and statue are the clues. This torch is a flame on a stick, like the Olympic torch. When a word has several meanings, test each one in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: A torch can be a small battery light that you hold in your hand. In America people call this a flashlight.
fact: A torch can also be a stick with a flame at the top, like the Olympic torch.
fact: To torch something means to set it on fire on purpose.
fact: Torchlight is the light that a torch gives out.
exercise: «In a power cut, use a torch, not a candle.» What is a torch in this sentence? | A stick with a flame at the top | *A small battery light you hold in your hand | To set something on fire | A kind of insect
exercise: «The statue of Liberty is holding up a torch, a gift from France.» What does torch mean here? | A small battery light | To set on fire | A map of the sea | *A flame on a stick, like the Olympic torch
exercise: «Never torch a field, because the fire can spread for miles.» What does torch mean? | A stick with a flame at the top | *To set on fire on purpose | A light for reading in bed | To carry a heavy bag
test: «Push the switch on a torch and the bulb lights.» In this sentence, what is a torch? | A flame on a stick | A kind of tree | To set on fire | *A small battery light you hold in your hand
test: «The arsonist planned to torch the empty barn.» What does torch mean here? | A small light for reading | *To set on fire on purpose | A stick with a flame at the top | Lost in the dark
exam: Which meaning of torch fits in «Shine the torch on the path so we can see the steps»? | *A small battery light you hold in your hand | A flame on a stick, like the Olympic torch | To set on fire on purpose | A heavy bag you carry on your back
